/*
Problem: Flatten Binary Tree to Linked List (LC 114)
Topic: Binary Tree / Reverse Preorder DFS

--------------------------------------------------

Idea:

Flatten the tree into a linked list
following Preorder order:

Root -> Left -> Right

Instead of building the list from
the front, process the tree in the
reverse order:

Right -> Left -> Root

Maintain a pointer (nextRight) to
the previously processed node.

For every node:

• Left child becomes NULL.

• Right child points to nextRight.

• Update nextRight to the current node.

--------------------------------------------------

Algorithm:

1. Traverse right subtree.

2. Traverse left subtree.

3. Set:

   root->left = NULL

   root->right = nextRight

4. Update:

   nextRight = root

--------------------------------------------------

Example:

        1
       / \
      2   5
     / \   \
    3   4   6

Reverse processing:

6

↓

5 -> 6

↓

4 -> 5 -> 6

↓

3 -> 4 -> 5 -> 6

↓

2 -> 3 -> 4 -> 5 -> 6

↓

1 -> 2 -> 3 -> 4 -> 5 -> 6

Final Tree:

1
 \
  2
   \
    3
     \
      4
       \
        5
         \
          6

--------------------------------------------------

Why It Works?

Processing in reverse preorder means
the next node in the final linked list
has already been built.

So every node simply attaches itself
to that previously processed node.

--------------------------------------------------

Time : O(n)

Every node is visited once.

Space : O(h)

h = height of tree
(recursion stack)

--------------------------------------------------

Pattern:

Reverse Preorder DFS
*/

class Solution {

    TreeNode* nextRight = NULL;

public:

    void flatten(TreeNode* root) {

        if (root == NULL)
            return;

        // Reverse preorder:
        // Right -> Left -> Root
        flatten(root->right);
        flatten(root->left);

        root->left = NULL;
        root->right = nextRight;

        nextRight = root;
    }
};
